[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Across the retrieved process experiences, the common failure pattern is acting before verifying preconditions. A find action can fail when the target object is unavailable, not visible, or unrecognized; this should be treated as evidence the object is not currently accessible, prompting exploration or an alternative rather than continued assumption. A pickup action can fail when the object is not present, not nearby, or not reachable, so the robot should first navigate to the object and confirm it is within reach. A move action can fail when an obstacle blocks the path, so the intended route should be checked and replanned around obstructions before moving. General principle: before each stage of the task, verify the relevant precondition (object exists and is visible, object is nearby/reachable for pickup, path is clear for movement, target location is reachable for placement), and if an action fails, diagnose the precondition failure and switch to exploration or replanning instead of proceeding as if success occurred.

## Preliminary Thinking
1) Inspect the current scene and known locations to determine whether a newspaper is present and visible. 2) If the newspaper is not found immediately, search likely areas or use exploration; if the find action fails, treat the newspaper as currently unavailable and continue exploring rather than assuming it can be used. 3) Once the newspaper is located, check the path to it and navigate toward it, replanning around any obstacles. 4) Confirm the newspaper is nearby and reachable before attempting pickup. 5) Pick up the newspaper. 6) Locate the couch, check the path to it and navigate there, replanning around obstacles. 7) Confirm the couch is reachable and that the placement surface is clear, then place the newspaper on the couch. 8) If any step fails, treat it as a precondition violation: diagnose whether the object, reachability, path, or placement area is the issue, and replan or explore accordingly.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]